SIRCL and RoCEnante
------------------
This core extracts transport mechanics from SparkRing's SIRCL and libsircl,
which derive from Local Inference Lab's b12x RoCEnante (b12x/comm/roce),
licensed under Apache-2.0. RoCEnante was written by Jason (original-el8) in
local-inference-lab/b12x PR 295, with dual-rail striping and graph-collective
work by Luke Alonso (lukealonso). b12x is developed in FlashInfer at
flashinfer/experimental/b12x. Preserve the provenance of derived source and
the original copyright notices when redistributing an extraction.

NVIDIA NCCL
-----------
The accompanying net-sircl plugin retains NVIDIA's Apache-2.0 network-plugin
headers and their notices: Copyright (c) 2017-2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION &
AFFILIATES. Its nccl/LICENSE.txt travels with the standalone bundle. The core
uses SparkRing transport implementation, not a newly copied NVIDIA NCCL
implementation. Consult net-sircl/NOTICE for its inherited source-reading
provenance. Vendored API headers were read to preserve compatibility.

Extraction origins
------------------
SIRCL/libsircl: SparkRing 947bce1e.
net-sircl: SparkRing 7b81b968.
src/topology.c and src/sysfs.c extract net-sircl's C topology/device helpers.
src/fabric.c extracts libsircl's transport planning; collective algorithms
remain in libsircl.
src/shm_verbs.c and include/sircl_core/emulation* own the shared-memory test
provider previously copied between libsircl and net-sircl. This provider is
test infrastructure, not a simulation of real relay capacity or performance.
src/verbs_dl.c retains libsircl's runtime-loaded verbs provider.
tools/adapt_proxy.py creates reviewed core-adapted compilations from pristine,
hash-checked SIRCL ABI9 proxy source; it does not alter the serving source.
